## Conversation
The user asked to make the dotfiles repository compatible with GitHub Dev Containers. They selected GitHub Codespaces personal dotfiles support and the existing install-all behavior, then asked to implement, commit, and push the change.

## Actions
Inspected the repository, history, existing notes, installers, shell configuration, and current GitHub Codespaces documentation. Added an executable install.sh that checks make and the Go version declared by clawbox/go.mod before running make install-all. Guarded Linux Homebrew initialization. Made Go installation failures propagate and removed the inaccurate fixed install path from the success message. Added Codespaces setup documentation while staging only that README section. Ran shellfmt, ShellCheck at error severity, Bash syntax checks, git diff checks, the complete Go test suite, a forced Go-install failure test, a Go 1.24 rejection test, and a public-only bootstrap in mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/go:1.25-bookworm. Created a signed commit. The post-commit hook rebased it onto the updated origin/master and pushed rebased commit 997b313.

## Errors & Mistakes
The first isolated HOME test was not isolated because Bash tilde expansion used the macOS account home. It refreshed the existing dotfile symlinks and installed clawbox under a temporary Go path. The 132 MB temporary directory was moved to Trash. Apple container initially lacked its default kernel, so the kernel was installed before container validation. The guessed image tag mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/go:1-1.25-bookworm returned 404; querying the registry with jq identified 1.25-bookworm. The first Go 1.25 assertion expected clawbox under $HOME/go/bin, but the image sets GOPATH=/go; the final test verified the executable through PATH. The automatic push was rejected because origin/master advanced. The hook rebased and pushed, but its autostash conflicted with the unrelated LiteLLM rewrite. Restored CLAUDE.md, README.md, and local-bin/litellm-proxy.sh byte-for-byte from the autostash, returned them to unstaged state, verified their hashes, and dropped the verified stash.

## Dead Ends
